{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4004230/extras/2e63484e2febe294c914a66af83c370a.avif?t=1768107945\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4004230/extras_big/2e63484e2febe294c914a66af83c370a.webp?t=1768107945 width=1560 height=882 /></span><i></i><br><br><br><i>Once Home</i> is an interactive 3D horror visual novel of slow dread and haunting beauty. You explore the Hemm residence at your own pace \u2014 observing, hovering, and uncovering traces of what has quietly altered the family and the place they once called home.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Burl and Eunice built this house with love \u2014 a refuge for their son Orin, his wife Hazel, and their child Rulon. For years, it was where the family came to feel whole again.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But something unseen lingers \u2014 patient, consuming, reshaping everything it touches. The air remembers. The rooms breathe. And the warmth that once filled this home now stirs with something unknown.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The deeper you step into the Hemm house, the more it asks of you \u2014 to feel, to face, to go further than you thought you would.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/4004230?t=1768107945","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/4004230?t=1768107945","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4004230/246ca1b53bba712f00bf78b5c8d0c5f39c530804/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1768107945","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4004230/246ca1b53bba712f00bf78b5c8d0c5f39c530804/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1768107945","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Playable without Timed Input","id":74},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[2,5],"notes":"ONCE HOME includes depictions and references to psychological distress, occult rituals, alien parasitic organisms, and moderate to strong scenes of gore and body horror. Some sequences may feature blood, ritual or medical procedures, and disturbing imagery. There is no explicit sexual content or nudity, though certain narrative elements may reference alien or distorted biological forms."},"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4004230/extras/2e63484e2febe294c914a66af83c370a.avif?t=1768107945\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4004230/extras_big/2e63484e2febe294c914a66af83c370a.webp?t=1768107945 width=1560 height=882 /></span><i></i><br><br><br><i>Once Home</i> is an interactive 3D horror visual novel of slow dread and haunting beauty. You explore the Hemm residence at your own pace \u2014 observing, hovering, and uncovering traces of what has quietly altered the family and the place they once called home.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Burl and Eunice built this house with love \u2014 a refuge for their son Orin, his wife Hazel, and their child Rulon. For years, it was where the family came to feel whole again.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But something unseen lingers \u2014 patient, consuming, reshaping everything it touches. The air remembers. The rooms breathe. And the warmth that once filled this home now stirs with something unknown.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The deeper you step into the Hemm house, the more it asks of you \u2014 to feel, to face, to go further than you thought you would.</p>","developers":["Ayan Pratap"],"genres":[{"description":"Indie","id":"23"},{"description":"Early Access","id":"70"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4004230/ca5db565a79e126e8747962d4f14ecd3f